Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Immediate network access for end devices.
2. Improves DHCP operation.
3. Faster user login.
4. Eliminates STP startup delay.
5. Works well with BPDU Guard.
6. Recommended on all access ports.
7. Improves user experience.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. Must not be enabled on switch-to-switch links.
2. Incorrect deployment may create loops.
3. Requires BPDU Guard for protection.
4. Misconfiguration can affect network stability.
5. Additional STP protections are still required.

Hence what came next
--------------------
PortFast protects access ports.

However, attackers may still manipulate STP topology by sending superior BPDUs.

Administrators wanted to protect STP against topology attacks and rogue root bridges.

This led to:

STP Attack Prevention

which combines:
- BPDU Guard
- Root Guard
- Loop Guard
- PortFast Security

to create a hardened STP environment.

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Configure Access Port

Switch(config)# interface fa0/1
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode access

Enable PortFast

Switch(config-if)# spanning-tree portfast

Enable BPDU Guard

Switch(config-if)# spanning-tree bpduguard enable


OR


Global Configuration

Switch(config)# spanning-tree portfast default

Switch(config)# spanning-tree portfast bpduguard default

Verification
============

show spanning-tree interface fa0/1 detail

show spanning-tree summary

show running-config interface fa0/1

